    "knowledge_point": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix",
    "problem": "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
